SU(2) factor-word wedge cumulative-cut audit

COMMAND
make -f Makefile.research probe_su2_factor_word_wedge_cuts
./probe_su2_factor_word_wedge_cuts 1000000 8 6

OUTPUT
SU2_FACTOR_WORD_WEDGE_CUTS samples=1000000 maximum_level=16 maximum_word_length=6 wedge_states=4999628 star_checks=28993748 star_failures=0 cut_flux_checks=28993748 cut_flux_failures=3302824 central_window_checks=15568816 central_window_failures=531055 star_prefix_checks=28993748 star_prefix_failures=0 star_suffix_checks=28993748 star_suffix_failures=0
FIRST_STAR_FAILURE level=-1 radius=-1 cut=-1 value=0 word=[] profile=[] square=[]
FIRST_CUT_FLUX_FAILURE level=4 radius=1 cut=1 value=-32 word=[1,2,2,1,1] profile=[1,3,1] square=[11,21,11]
FIRST_CENTRAL_WINDOW_FAILURE level=6 radius=1 cut=1 value=-204 word=[2,3,1,1,2] profile=[2,6,6,3] square=[85,204,204,84]
FIRST_STAR_PREFIX_FAILURE level=-1 radius=-1 cut=-1 value=0 word=[] profile=[] square=[]
FIRST_STAR_SUFFIX_FAILURE level=-1 radius=-1 cut=-1 value=0 word=[] profile=[] square=[]

METHOD
For each deterministic arbitrary-factor word, the audit constructs its
half-profile p, fusion square d=p^2, and multiplication kernel C=N_d.
For every source radius R it constructs the exact propagated wedge

  W_R(i,j)=d_i C_(j,R)-d_j C_(i,R).

The star coordinates W_R(0,S) are the anchored currents.  The audit
also checks the unweighted cut fluxes

  sum_(i<=t<j) W_R(i,j)

and the sums over every reflected central wedge window.  It uses
arbitrary-precision integers throughout.

The first cut-flux failure is an exact actual-orbit example at K=2:
p=(1,3,1), d=(11,21,11), and R=1.  The cut t=1 consists of
W_1(0,2)+W_1(1,2)=0-32=-32.

The first reflected-window failure is at K=3:
p=(2,6,6,3), d=(85,204,204,84), and R=1.  The depth-one window
contains only W_1(1,2)=-204.

Thus neither unweighted order-cut fluxes nor reflected central-window
sums define the missing cumulative invariant cone.  The zero star
failures are bounded evidence for the target, not its proof.

